# Later rules win, so the general case comes first and the exceptions follow.

* text=auto

*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The sample CSV files are fixtures whose exact bytes are the point of them:
# crlf.csv proves Windows line endings survive, utf8-bom.csv proves a byte-order
# mark is preserved, windows-1252.csv proves a non-UTF-8 encoding is not
# silently converted. Git must not normalise any of them, or the tests that
# check byte-for-byte fidelity would be comparing against already-altered files.
test/resources/samples/** -text -diff
